WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.360
Jeremy Renner may no longer have his own app,&nbsp;
but hey, now he has his own show! "Hawkeye" on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.000
Disney+ is very fun, but after the first two&nbsp;
episodes, we have questions. Like, what's up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.960
with Kate Bishop's mom's fiance's uncle's&nbsp;
death? And who's a good boy? Let's explore!

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.880
“Hawkeye” Episode 1 starts off&nbsp;
with a bang — or hundreds of them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.160
you could say — as we’re transported back&nbsp;
in time to the Battle of New York from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.760
original “Avengers” film. After we get a&nbsp;
brief glimpse into the shaky marriage of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.000
young Kate Bishop’s parents Eleanor and Derek&nbsp;
Bishop, their swanky penthouse starts shaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.600
and eventually crumbling as the Chitauri&nbsp;
decimate the buildings of New York.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.200
A young Kate is on her own in the penthouse&nbsp;
as she gets separated from her parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.120
and a Chitarui almost takes her out, but we&nbsp;
see that an arrow from Hawkeye takes down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.520
the small alien ship before it claims her. Kate&nbsp;
spots Hawkeye on the roof of a nearby building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.960
identifying her savior, who then leaps&nbsp;
from the building and shoots a grapple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.000
arrow — a throwback to a famous&nbsp;
Clint moment from “The Avengers.”

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.480
It’s at this moment that Kate becomes inspired,&nbsp;
thanks to the heroic efforts of Hawkeye on that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.720
roof. He saved her life, and she admits to her&nbsp;
mom at her father’s funeral that she wants a bow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:05.280
and arrow. Thanks to Hawkeye’s heroism that day in&nbsp;
New York, Kate takes up archery and other skills,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.840
including karate and fencing. Without Clint,&nbsp;
there would be no Kate Bishop in the MCU.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.240
One of the goals of Episode 1 of “Hawkeye”&nbsp;
is to explain to the viewer what’s going on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.400
with Clint since we last saw him in “Avengers:&nbsp;
Endgame.” It’s been more than two years since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:23.120
his last MCU scene as he attended Tony Stark’s&nbsp;
funeral, but he was reunited with his family.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.120
He is still with his kids as “Hawkeye” kicks&nbsp;
off, as we see the foursome attend “Rogers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.800
The Musical” without mom. Watching the&nbsp;
silly musical turns out to be slightly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.560
triggering for Clint, who clearly is&nbsp;
annoyed at the nonsense of it all.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:41.880
"Honey, I know what happens. I was there. You&nbsp;
know who wasn't there? It's that guy. Ant-Man."

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.240
He’s mostly in his feelings about&nbsp;
the loss of his best friend Natasha,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.880
as we see his mind wander after the musical&nbsp;
version Natasha starts cart-wheeling around.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.680
It’s here that he takes a break&nbsp;
and leaves to go to the restroom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.880
and we also see him fumble with his&nbsp;
hearing aid. It turns out Clint has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.040
suffered some severe hearing loss in his left&nbsp;
ear thanks to his adventures with the Avengers.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.720
It looks like Clint is making up for lost&nbsp;
time with his kids and is spending the days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.320
leading up to Christmas with them. Laura is&nbsp;
off at their farmhouse and explains their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.640
separation by suggesting this is supposed&nbsp;
to be Clint’s one-on-one time with his kids.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.160
Of course, Clint is pulled away from&nbsp;
his family after spotting Kate on TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.840
in the Ronin suit from “Avengers: Endgame.”

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.160
We’re introduced to two villains in&nbsp;
the first episode of “Hawkeye.” One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.840
is the Tracksuit Mafia, who are truly&nbsp;
living up to their Marvel Comics hype.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.800
We don’t really get a sense of who&nbsp;
they are and why they’re so angry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.520
but we do know that they had run-ins with Ronin&nbsp;
when he was on his killing rampage after The Snap.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.280
They chase down Kate after she fumbles their&nbsp;
heist of the secret black market auction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:40.960
but Clint comes to save the day after he&nbsp;
sees his Ronin suit back on the streets of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.280
New York. Kate snatched it during the auction&nbsp;
chaos while Jack made off with Ronin’s sword.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:48.480
Speaking of Jack, this is another&nbsp;
villain we need to keep our eye on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.200
He has suspiciously wooed Kate’s widow mother,&nbsp;
and the pair are now engaged. He loves swords,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.080
which is no surprise given Jack is pulled directly&nbsp;
from the Marvel Comics character Jacques Duquesne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:02.560
aka Swordsman. A former mentor and teacher&nbsp;
of Clint, Jaques has no connection with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.240
Kate Bishop in the comics, so this is an&nbsp;
interesting twist “Hawkeye” is giving us.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:10.720
While we don’t know what Jack is up to in Episode&nbsp;
1, his creepiness alone lets us know he is up to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.720
no good. It’s already suspected that he’s&nbsp;
involved in the death of his uncle Armand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.840
and there's some talk at the&nbsp;
auction of a sizable inheritance.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.920
While Episode 1 served as an&nbsp;
introduction to Kate, her mother Eleanor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.720
Jack, the Tracksuit Mafia — oh, and we can’t&nbsp;
forget Lucky the Pizza Dog! — it gave us a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.080
good idea of where “Hawkeye” is going and&nbsp;
themes that will be carried throughout.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:34.320
Clint is clearly still dealing with the grief&nbsp;
of losing Natasha, while he also seems to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:38.880
trying to cover up his past as Ronin. He still&nbsp;
has enemies from his days as the vigilante,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.320
and they’re coming back to haunt him&nbsp;
thanks to his number one fan, Kate.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:46.320
Kate, a vigilante in her own right, is now&nbsp;
working to uncover the mystery of her future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:51.360
step-dad and the murder of Armand III (who, in&nbsp;
the comics, is actually Jack’s father). She’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:55.920
become the target of the Tracksuit Mafia, who&nbsp;
clearly are not the men in charge. We suspect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.680
Kate and Clint will find out they somehow&nbsp;
have a connection to one another, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:03.600
given how all these characters intertwine in&nbsp;
the comics. And then there's the lingering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:08.320
mystery of that watch, which is very important&nbsp;
to the Tracksuit Mafia for some unknown reason.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.320
"We have 90 seconds to find the&nbsp;
watch. Everything else is secondary."

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:17.200
Episode 2 picks up immediately after Episode&nbsp;
1, as Clint Barton is pulling the Ronin mask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.800
off of Kate Bishop in an alley. Clint is&nbsp;
keen on getting his suit back from Kate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.040
so they head to her apartment&nbsp;
to hide out for a moment.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:27.040
While still in shock that she’s with the real&nbsp;
Hawkeye, Kate changes and hands the suit over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:31.520
to Clint. Unfortunately, those pesky Tracksuit&nbsp;
Mafia members have tracked them down and start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:36.080
throwing Molotov cocktails through her apartment&nbsp;
window. The apartment eventually catches fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:40.160
causing the duo to abandon the Ronin suit,&nbsp;
and now Kate and Clint are on the run.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.520
Once the Tracksuit Mafia sets&nbsp;
Kate’s apartment on fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:47.680
the duo has to bolt and head somewhere safe.&nbsp;
Kate decides to go to her aunt’s apartment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:51.760
since she's out of town. Clint forces Kate to&nbsp;
hide out there while he heads back to retrieve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:55.920
the suit. He finds out one of the firemen&nbsp;
stole it, which is just another unnecessary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:00.320
obstacle for Clint to overcome. He comes back&nbsp;
to visit Kate and helps her patch up a wound,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.680
and we get a peek at how Clint might&nbsp;
become a father figure to his new friend.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:06.800
The following day, Clint has to ditch&nbsp;
his kids as he sends them off to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.480
with their very understanding mom. He&nbsp;
revisits Kate back at their hideout,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:13.920
and then they go their separate ways&nbsp;
but not before exchanging phone numbers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:18.800
Clint thinks this is the last time he’ll see Kate&nbsp;
and begs her only to call if she has an emergency.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:23.040
It’s now Clint’s mission to retrieve the Ronin&nbsp;
suit and figure out why the Tracksuit Mafia is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:27.520
stirring up trouble yet again. He travels to a&nbsp;
live-action role-play event to find his suit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:30.400
where he suspects the thieving&nbsp;
firefighter will be wearing it.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.520
Clint must sign up and participate in&nbsp;
the event to get to the firefighter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:37.200
which turns into one of the best&nbsp;
slow-motion bits ever to be seen in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.200
as Clint (fake) slices and dices&nbsp;
some hilarious adversaries. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:44.560
a duel with the thief, Clint is finally&nbsp;
in possession of the Ronin suit again.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:50.000
Back at Kate’s mom’s penthouse, Jack is back&nbsp;
doing very Jack things. He continues to fool&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:54.320
Kate’s mom while not fooling his soon-to-be&nbsp;
daughter-in-law, but he also doesn’t seem to care.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:58.400
Kate ends up challenging him to a fencing match,&nbsp;
where he pretends to be the lesser competitor.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.680
As Kate yells at Jack to stop letting&nbsp;
her win, she eventually tricks him into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:06.320
showing off his true talent and uses this&nbsp;
as a way to prove he’s some kind of liar.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.000
"Sorry for scaring you into telling the truth."

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:13.840
Obviously Jack is a liar, but we’re still&nbsp;
not sure what his true intentions are.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:17.360
He's still in possession of the Ronin&nbsp;
sword, but it's unclear what his plan is.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:22.000
After his fencing match with Kate, he offers her&nbsp;
a butterscotch, one which matches those in a bowl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:27.040
at Armand's house from Episode 1. This appears to&nbsp;
be enough proof for Kate that Jack killed Armand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:30.880
but in reality, all it suggests is that&nbsp;
Jack has been to his Uncle’s house before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:35.280
Jack's involvement with his uncle's death is&nbsp;
still unclear, but things don't look good.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:40.640
While Kate is having some family fun, Clint sets&nbsp;
himself up to be kidnapped by the Tracksuit Mafia.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:45.040
He tells his wife on the phone that he’s doing&nbsp;
a catch and release, which Laura points out is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:49.120
“Classic Nat.” After luring the goons to&nbsp;
him, Clint is taken to a secret location,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:52.720
where he continues to tell the gangsters&nbsp;
he wants to talk to the person in charge.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:56.960
After realizing Clint’s in trouble, Kate comes&nbsp;
to help after tracking his location but falls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:00.720
through the roof of the building and causes&nbsp;
a mess instead. As Kate and Clint are tied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:04.720
up by the gang, one of the mafia members goes&nbsp;
into a speaker-filled room to get the boss.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:09.920
As the bass in the background booms, we&nbsp;
get our first look at Maya Lopez, aka Echo.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:14.720
It’s the briefest of glimpses as the screen cuts&nbsp;
to credits after we see her face, but it promises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:19.840
us an even bigger episode for next week. Echo,&nbsp;
who already has her own series coming to Disney+,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:24.000
is a deaf hero who is mainly known for her&nbsp;
role in the “Daredevil” comics. The adoptive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.440
daughter of Kingpin, Echo’s appearance&nbsp;
in “Hawkeye” might hint that we could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:31.440
be getting a second go-round with Wilson&nbsp;
Fisk from the Netflix “Daredevil” series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:35.360
Or the MCU could remix her origin the way&nbsp;
it's done with plenty of other heroes.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:38.800
While it looks like Echo is the villain&nbsp;
now, we can almost guarantee she won’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:43.040
be. There is either a bigger threat we&nbsp;
haven’t met, or Jack truly is the big bad.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:46.880
The biggest takeaway from “Hawkeye”&nbsp;
Episode 2? Still no Yelena Belova&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:50.640
from "Black Widow," as promised, but we&nbsp;
expect she's right around the corner.

